          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "jiàoxun is built from jiào and xùn, both inherited from Middle Chinese, kaewH and xjunH (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'to teach' and the second 'to admonish'. The second is said light here."
            }
